      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "Now that we added our styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "in our navigation bar let's work on the pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 10.48,
          "en": "Let's maybe start with the \"All meetups\" page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.48,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "and let's output a list of dummy meetups for the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.55,
          "end": 19.3,
          "en": "before we then make sure that we can add our own meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.434,
          "end": 23.63,
          "en": "And for this I'll go to the all meetups js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.63,
          "end": 28.63,
          "en": "And the goal in there is to get a list of meetups later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.35,
          "end": 33.36,
          "en": "we will get it from a server by sending a HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 33.36,
          "end": 37.23,
          "en": "for the moment we'll work with some dummy meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 40.19,
          "en": "And I then went to output those meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.19,
          "end": 41.79,
          "en": "Now for this I'll, first of all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 46.43,
          "en": "add a constant name, dummy data, which we'll replace later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 46.43,
          "end": 48.853,
          "en": "which holds an array of dummy meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 49.97,
          "end": 52.64,
          "en": "Now here I'll just add a bunch of JavaScript objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.64,
          "end": 55.64,
          "en": "which hold the meetup data, things like the image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.64,
          "end": 59.67,
          "en": "the title, the description text and the address maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.67,
          "end": 62.19,
          "en": "And for this you can definitely also use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 64.24,
          "en": "my code attachments there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 64.24,
          "end": 66.96,
          "en": "you'll find some prepared, dummy data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.96,
          "end": 69.07,
          "en": "You can also prepare it your own one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.07,
          "end": 71.55,
          "en": "Here I just have two dummy objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.55,
          "end": 75.37,
          "en": "which have basically the same content, just different id's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 75.37,
          "end": 79.1,
          "en": "and different titles, but the same image, the same address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.1,
          "end": 82.14,
          "en": "the same description text, because of course it's not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.14,
          "end": 85.9,
          "en": "about the dummy data, but about what we do with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 85.9,
          "end": 88.01,
          "en": "Now, one word about that image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.01,
          "end": 90.34,
          "en": "I got that from Wikipedia.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.34,
          "end": 92.66,
          "en": "You can of course bring your own images.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.66,
          "end": 96.86,
          "en": "Here I got this nice looking image here created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.86,
          "end": 99.42,
          "en": "by Thomas Wolf and not by me.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.42,
          "end": 102.91,
          "en": "So just to give him, due credits.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.91,
          "end": 104.92,
          "en": "And you can of course bring your own image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.92,
          "end": 108.85,
          "en": "Just make sure that you simply get a URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.85,
          "end": 111.09,
          "en": "to some image and store that in this image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.09,
          "end": 113.793,
          "en": "property of your dummy data points.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 114.72999999999999,
          "end": 116.53,
          "en": "Now we got the dummy data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.53,
          "end": 119.43,
          "en": "now the goal is to output that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.43,
          "end": 124.34,
          "en": "So for this here in this div or section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.34,
          "end": 128.32,
          "en": "which we could also use, we can add an h1 tag let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.32,
          "end": 132.6,
          "en": "and say \"all meetups\" then below that we want to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.6,
          "end": 137.47,
          "en": "output this data, but of course not as code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.47,
          "end": 140.57,
          "en": "but instead as JSX elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.57,
          "end": 144.97,
          "en": "And for this we now need to learn how we can render a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.97,
          "end": 149.4,
          "en": "of JSX elements, dynamically, how we can translate a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 149.4,
          "end": 152.91,
          "en": "of data into a list of JSX elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.91,
          "end": 157.49,
          "en": "Because it is worth noting that in JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.49,
          "end": 162.13,
          "en": "you can actually render an array JSX elements like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 162.13,
          "end": 165.44,
          "en": "So output a dynamic expression with curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.44,
          "end": 167.07,
          "en": "then add an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.07,
          "end": 171.06,
          "en": "And in there you could have list items like item one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 171.06,
          "end": 173.143,
          "en": "and then as a second item, item two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.54,
          "end": 177.1,
          "en": "And if you do that, those are rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.1,
          "end": 182.1,
          "en": "So arrays are rendered correctly, automatically by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.92,
          "end": 185.9,
          "en": "And that's important to know, because that means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.9,
          "end": 189.15,
          "en": "that if we can translate this array of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.15,
          "end": 193.69,
          "en": "into an array of JSX elements, we can output it down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 193.69,
          "end": 196.25,
          "en": "And there is a way for translating",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.25,
          "end": 200.65,
          "en": "an array into an array of different data in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 200.65,
          "end": 203.66,
          "en": "On that dummy data array, we can call the built in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.66,
          "end": 207.45,
          "en": "map method, which exists in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.45,
          "end": 211.03,
          "en": "And map allows us to execute a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.03,
          "end": 215.1,
          "en": "here I'm writing an arrow function on every element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.1,
          "end": 219,
          "en": "in that array, and it will get this element as a input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 219,
          "end": 222.38,
          "en": "So in this case the meetup let's say as a input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 222.38,
          "end": 225.40699999999998,
          "en": "automatically because this function is called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.40699999999998,
          "end": 227.78,
          "en": "\"Automatically by JavaScript\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.78,
          "end": 231.12,
          "en": "and we then return the transformed data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 231.12,
          "end": 235.63,
          "en": "And the result of calling map then is a new array full",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.63,
          "end": 238.16,
          "en": "of that transformed data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.16,
          "end": 240.99,
          "en": "And here we could say for every meetup object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.99,
          "end": 244.88,
          "en": "which we're getting, we want to return a list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 244.88,
          "end": 247.12,
          "en": "And hence we may be actually wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 247.12,
          "end": 250.1,
          "en": "as all here with an unordered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 250.1,
          "end": 251.4,
          "en": "And in that list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.4,
          "end": 254.88,
          "en": "we want to output data about that meetup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.88,
          "end": 258.87,
          "en": "for example to begin with, to output the title.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 262.33,
          "en": "So here I'm dynamically outputting meetup title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 262.33,
          "end": 264.053,
          "en": "in this JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 265.3,
          "end": 267.75,
          "en": "So with that, we transform our array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.75,
          "end": 271.283,
          "en": "of objects into an array of li elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 272.17,
          "end": 275.46,
          "en": "And if we do that, just like this, and we reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.46,
          "end": 278.75,
          "en": "we see this is a first and this is a second meetup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.75,
          "end": 280.653,
          "en": "So that does work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 282.02,
          "end": 285.43,
          "en": "Now, there is one important note about lists, though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 285.43,
          "end": 289.21,
          "en": "if you open the developer tools, you'll see a warning here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 289.21,
          "end": 292.713,
          "en": "that each child in a list should have a unique \"key\" prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 293.67,
          "end": 296.01,
          "en": "That is a requirement by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 296.01,
          "end": 300.88,
          "en": "which it needs to update and render lists efficiently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 300.88,
          "end": 303.72,
          "en": "I dive deeper into that in my React course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 303.72,
          "end": 305.32,
          "en": "for the moment it's enough to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 305.32,
          "end": 308.6,
          "en": "that we should add the \"key\" prop here to the list item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.6,
          "end": 313.5,
          "en": "and then set this to some unique value per item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 313.5,
          "end": 316.68,
          "en": "And we have a unique value for every list item here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 316.68,
          "end": 320.84,
          "en": "the IDs, the IDs are different for every item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 320.84,
          "end": 323.54,
          "en": "So here we can then set this to meetup.id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 324.45,
          "end": 328.743,
          "en": "and with that we'll no longer get that warning if we reload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 329.96,
          "end": 332.1,
          "en": "So that is how we can render a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 332.1,
          "end": 334.77,
          "en": "of data simply by mapping it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 334.77,
          "end": 338.3,
          "en": "And that is how you typically do render lists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 338.3,
          "end": 340.6,
          "en": "of data with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 340.6,
          "end": 343.5,
          "en": "But in the end, you can just render any array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 343.5,
          "end": 347.853,
          "en": "of JSX elements, no matter how you derived that array.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
